      "content": "One-sided swelling with warmth and redness is a classic sign of a deep vein thrombosis (DVT), which is a medical emergency that can be fatal if a clot travels to your lungs.\nYou are absolutely right to be worried, and this is not a normal strain; a strain would not cause significant redness or heat.\nStop taking the Ibuprofen immediately and go to the ER or call 911 right now to get an ultrasound done before you have a heart attack or pulmonary embolism.",
